[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMCBOOT-15
TITLE: Flash Memory Processing
STATEMENT: >>>
The platform flash map exposes an 800 KiB primary image slot at `0x00432000`, an 800 KiB secondary
image slot at `0x004FA000`, and a 64 KiB scratch area at `0x005C2000`. The flash backend reports
8 KiB erase sectors to MCUboot and performs page-aligned 512-byte read-modify-write operations for
arbitrary flash-area writes.

During upload, MCUboot progressively erases only secondary-slot sectors required by incoming data.
During a confirmed upgrade, MCUboot exchanges the primary and secondary images using the scratch
area. The bootloader flash region is not exposed through the mcumgr image-upload mapping.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-3
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-4
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMCBOOT-16
TITLE: Image Authentication and Upgrade
STATEMENT: >>>
The bootloader embeds an ECDSA P-256 public key and uses TinyCrypt to verify image signatures.
The build process signs application images with the matching private key. The image list service
reports only images that pass MCUboot validation; therefore a completed upload is not accepted as
a successful update until the secondary image appears with a hash and is confirmed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-7
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-8
  ROLE: Refines

[DESIGN_ITEM]
UID: SW-H1FWMCBOOT-17
TITLE: Recovery Request
STATEMENT: >>>
The main application writes a magic value to general-purpose backup register zero before a software
reset in response to `*BOOTL\n`. The bootloader compares this value during startup, clears it before
entering serial recovery, and otherwise proceeds with normal image validation. This prevents stray
UART data from entering serial recovery indefinitely.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RQ-H1FWMCBOOT-6
  ROLE: Refines

